\ Regression tests for exact non-recursive month weaving shortcuts.
\ All test values were independently verified against the full recurrence.
\ The two-month examples need no memo records.
\ For 47 already-started months, the result is 93 double factorial,
\ equal to the product of the odd numbers 1,3,...,93 (73 digits).
\ These are pending CAL compilation and native execution.

To check the two-month closed weaving counts:
  Prepare two synthetic months.
  Count all possible month weavings.
  If the weaving selection's total completions is not "20",
    put "The closed two-month initial count should be twenty." into the check report; exit.
  If the weaving selection's memo entry count is not 0,
    put "Two-month counting unexpectedly allocated memo records." into the check report; exit.
  Find the woven month state given 1.
  Put 3 into the examined woven month state's remaining days.
  Put 7 into the weaving selection's days remaining.
  Count weaving completions into a short check wide quantity.
  If the short check wide quantity is not "20",
    put "The first started month has an incorrect closed count." into the check report; exit.
  Find the woven month state given 2.
  Put 3 into the examined woven month state's remaining days.
  Put 6 into the weaving selection's days remaining.
  Count weaving completions into the short check wide quantity.
  If the short check wide quantity is not "10",
    put "Two started unfinished months should have ten completions." into the check report; exit.
  Find the woven month state given 1.
  Put 4 into the examined woven month state's remaining days.
  Put 7 into the weaving selection's days remaining.
  Count weaving completions into the short check wide quantity.
  If the short check wide quantity is not "0",
    put "A later started month cannot precede an unstarted earlier month." into the check report; exit.
  Find the woven month state given 1.
  Put 0 into the examined woven month state's remaining days.
  Find the woven month state given 2.
  Put 4 into the examined woven month state's remaining days.
  Put 4 into the weaving selection's days remaining.
  Count weaving completions into the short check wide quantity.
  If the short check wide quantity is not "1",
    put "A single unfinished month does not have one continuation." into the check report; exit.
  If the weaving selection's memo entry count is not 0,
    put "Closed two-month cases used the sparse memo unnecessarily." into the check report; exit.

To set the first three woven remaining counts to two:
  Put 1 into a checked month ordinal number.
  Loop.
    If the checked month ordinal number is greater than 3, break.
    Find the woven month state given the checked month ordinal number.
    Put 2 into the examined woven month state's remaining days.
    Add 1 to the checked month ordinal number.
  Repeat.

To check the all-started weaving product:
  Prepare three synthetic months.
  Count all possible month weavings.
  Set the first three woven remaining counts to two.
  Put 6 into the weaving selection's days remaining.
  Count weaving completions into a started check wide quantity.
  If the started check wide quantity is not "15",
    put "Three started months with two days each have an incorrect product." into the check report; exit.
  Prepare four synthetic months.
  Count all possible month weavings.
  Set the first three woven remaining counts to two.
  Find the woven month state given 4.
  Put 2 into the examined woven month state's remaining days.
  Put 8 into the weaving selection's days remaining.
  Count weaving completions into the started check wide quantity.
  If the started check wide quantity is not "105",
    put "Four started months with two days each have an incorrect product." into the check report; exit.

To check a forty seven month started suffix:
  Destroy the chosen month lengths.
  Put 47 into the selected month count.
  Put 1 into a synthetic month number.
  Loop.
    If the synthetic month number is greater than 47, break.
    Add a synthetic month with 4.
    Add 1 to the synthetic month number.
  Repeat.
  Prepare the woven month states.
  Put the woven month states' first into a stress month state.
  Loop.
    If the stress month state is nil, break.
    Put 2 into the stress month state's remaining days.
    Put the stress month state's next into the stress month state.
  Repeat.
  Put 94 into the weaving selection's days remaining.
  Put 0 into the weaving selection's resource limit reached.
  Count weaving completions into a stress wide quantity.
  If the stress wide quantity is not "2987435000850314871976096554696085799164511452611632783323554397412109375",
    put "Forty seven started months lost precision in their final-order count." into the check report; exit.
  If the weaving selection's resource limit reached is not 0,
    put "The direct forty seven month calculation reached the resource limit." into the check report; exit.
